(text "X1 is a LOGICAL interface, not a new 11-pin connector.\nExisting mic / amplifier / OLED / buttons retain their wiring.\nPeripheral power and auxiliary pins are not reconstructed.\nDo not infer module VCC or speaker grounding from this sheet." (at 231.14 198.12 0) (effects (font (size 1.651 1.651)) (justify left top)) (uuid f995e1b7-5ec2-5043-bb9d-e0eef4885f57))
(text "BOOT: dry contact to system ground; parallel to on-board BOOT.\nIt stops software actions. It does NOT isolate actuator power.\nHolding BOOT during reset may select ROM download mode.\nNo external pull-up / RC values are frozen here." (at 20.32 203.2 0) (effects (font (size 1.651 1.651)) (justify left top)) (uuid 412db020-4921-5c57-ad13-ed2a3532a80e))
(text "PIN ID: IO8 = GPIO8; [L12] = photo-based header position.\nComponent side facing you, antenna UP, USB DOWN.\nL/R rows counted 1-22 from antenna to USB; verify continuity.\nNo new encoder / ultrasonic / servo GPIO allocation." (at 20.32 238.76 0) (effects (font (size 1.651 1.651)) (justify left top)) (uuid 5ad4a919-7068-57b5-9dfa-6c68f0b50f55))
(text "Source: action_outputs.h + cybertrack_tools.cc (ct19).\nRetained peripherals: bread-compact-wifi/config.h.\nFirmware pin identity does not prove physical wiring.\nA1: no PCB transfer; see parameter-confirmation.md (E01-E10)." (at 231.14 238.76 0) (effects (font (size 1.651 1.651)) (justify left top)) (uuid 431051d3-d195-5244-aad8-b7e9d83c706d))
)
